.Dd March 2, 2026
.Dt ELF_INIT_MIPS64 3
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm elf_init_mips64
.Nd create a new ELF relocatable object configured for MIPS64
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libelfobj
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In elfobj.h
.Ft elfobj_t *
.Fn elf_init_mips64 void
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn elf_init_mips64
function allocates a mutable
.Vt elfobj_t
and initializes it for MIPS64 relocatable output.
.Pp
The created object uses:
.Bl -tag -width "Architecture flags"
.It ELF type
.Dv ET_REL
.It Machine
.Dv EM_MIPS
.It Class
.Dv ELFCLASS64
.It Data encoding
.Dv ELFDATA2LSB
.It Architecture flags
.Dv EF_MIPS_ABI_O64 | EF_MIPS_ARCH_64R2
.El
.Pp
Default sections are created as part of initialization:
.Pa .text
(alignment 8),
.Pa .data
(alignment 8), and
.Pa .bss
(alignment 8).
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn elf_init_mips64
function returns a pointer to a newly allocated object on success.
On failure, it returns
.Dv NULL .
.Sh EXAMPLE
.Bd -literal
elfobj_t *obj = elf_init_mips64();
if (obj == NULL)
    errx(1, "elf_init_mips64 failed");
/* populate object */
elf_close(obj);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr elf_close 3 ,
.Xr elf_finalize 3 ,
.Xr elfobj 3
